2958	210	9	five_statement_truth	Select the correct statement regarding plant transport mechanisms and translocation.	\N	Sucrose loading into companion cells/sieve tubes at source regions requires active transport mediated by ATP-driven proton pumps and sucrose-H+ symporters. Tracheary elements are dead at maturity (no metabolic energy). Pressure-flow moves sap from higher to lower hydrostatic pressure. Guttation occurs through hydathodes, not stomata. Cavitation disrupts water columns.	1	apply	moderate	["A. Transpiration pull is the primary force for water movement in the xylem and requires metabolic energy expended directly by tracheary elements.", "B. The pressure-flow hypothesis explains that organic solutes move through phloem from a source with lower hydrostatic pressure to a sink with higher hydrostatic pressure.", "C. Guttation occurs through stomata during periods of high transpiration and high soil moisture.", "D. Loading of sucrose into companion cells and sieve tube elements at the source involves active transport utilizing proton pumps.", "E. Cavitation in xylem vessels enhances the upward movement of water columns under high negative pressure."]	D	\N	\N	null	null	null	null	2026-08-16 19:21:24.245809	\N	{"id": 2958, "points": 1.0, "exam_id": 210, "options": ["A. Transpiration pull is the primary force for water movement in the xylem and requires metabolic energy expended directly by tracheary elements.", "B. The pressure-flow hypothesis explains that organic solutes move through phloem from a source with lower hydrostatic pressure to a sink with higher hydrostatic pressure.", "C. Guttation occurs through stomata during periods of high transpiration and high soil moisture.", "D. Loading of sucrose into companion cells and sieve tube elements at the source involves active transport utilizing proton pumps.", "E. Cavitation in xylem vessels enhances the upward movement of water columns under high negative pressure."], "stem_text": "Select the correct stateme