2968	210	19	combination_grid	Which of the following statements regarding the human nervous system and nerve impulse transmission are correct?\n\nA. The resting membrane potential of a neuron is maintained primarily by the sodium-potassium pump actively transporting 3 Na⁺ out and 2 K⁺ in.\nB. During depolarization of an axon membrane, voltage-gated potassium channels open rapidly while sodium channels remain closed.\nC. Saltatory conduction occurs in myelinated nerve fibers where action potentials jump from one Node of Ranvier to the next.\nD. Neurotransmitters are released from the presynaptic knob into the synaptic cleft via exocytosis upon the influx of calcium ions.	\N	Statement A is correct (sodium-potassium pump mechanism). Statement B is incorrect because during depolarization, voltage-gated sodium channels open rapidly, not potassium channels (potassium channels open during repolarization). Statement C is correct (saltatory conduction in myelinated fibers). Statement D is correct (calcium-mediated exocytosis of neurotransmitters). Therefore, A, C, and D are correct.	1	apply	moderate	["A. A, B and C only", "B. B, C and D only", "C. A, B and D only", "D. A, C and D only", "E. All A, B, C and D are correct"]	D	\N	\N	[{"id": "A", "text": "The resting membrane potential of a neuron is maintained primarily by the sodium-potassium pump actively transporting 3 Na\\u207a out and 2 K\\u207a in.", "is_true": true}, {"id": "B", "text": "During depolarization of an axon membrane, voltage-gated potassium channels open rapidly while sodium channels remain closed.", "is_true": false}, {"id": "C", "text": "Saltatory conduction occurs in myelinated nerve fibers where action potentials jump from one Node of Ranvier to the next.", "is_true": true}, {"id": "D", "text": "Neurotransmitters are released from the presynaptic knob into the synaptic cleft via exocytosis upon the influx of calcium ions.", "is_true": true}]	null	null	null	2026-08-16 19:21:24.245827	\N	{"id": 2968, "point