2971	210	22	five_statement_truth	Which of the following statements regarding environmental biology, ecological pyramids, and biogeochemical cycles in Sri Lankan ecosystems is correct?	\N	Statement D is correct: non-biodegradable, lipid-soluble toxins (such as heavy metals or persistent pesticides) undergo biomagnification, increasing in concentration at higher trophic levels. Statement A is false because aquatic biomass pyramids can be inverted (phytoplankton biomass < zooplankton biomass). Statement B is false because energy flows one-way while nutrients cycle. Statement C is false because nitrogen-fixing bacteria convert N₂ into ammonia/ammonium (NH3/NH4+), not nitrites directly. Statement E describes secondary succession, not primary succession.	1	apply	moderate	["A. In all aquatic ecosystems, the ecological pyramid of biomass is invariably upright because producers have a shorter life span and higher turnover rate than consumers.", "B. Biological magnification (biomagnification) results in higher concentrations of persistent lipophilic toxins in organisms at higher trophic levels.", "C. The flow of energy through an ecosystem is cyclical, whereas nutrients follow a one-way unidirectional flow.", "D. Nitrogen fixation converts atmospheric nitrogen gas directly into nitrites (NO2-) which are then absorbed by plant roots.", "E. Primary succession always begins on a pre-existing soil substrate after a forest fire or agricultural clearing."]	B	\N	\N	null	null	null	null	2026-08-16 19:21:24.245832	\N	{"id": 2971, "points": 1.0, "exam_id": 210, "options": ["A. In all aquatic ecosystems, the ecological pyramid of biomass is invariably upright because producers have a shorter life span and higher turnover rate than consumers.", "B. Biological magnification (biomagnification) results in higher concentrations of persistent lipophilic toxins in organisms at higher trophic levels.", "C. The flow of energy through an ecosystem is cyclical, whereas nutrients follow a one-way unidirectional flow.", "D. Nitrogen fixation converts atmospheric nitrogen gas directly into nitrites (NO2-) which are then absorbed by plant roots.", "E. Primary succession always begins on a pre-existing soil substrate after a forest fire or agricultural clearing."], "stem_text": "Which of the following statements regarding environmental biology, ecological pyramids, and biogeochemical cycles in Sri Lankan ecosystems is correct?", "difficulty": "moderate", "diagram_url": null, "explanation": "Statement D is correct: non-biodegradable, lipid-soluble toxins (such as heavy metals or persistent pesticides) undergo biomagnification, increasing in concentration at higher trophic levels. Statement A is false because aquatic biomass pyramids can be inverted (phytoplankton biomass < zooplankton biomass). Statement B is false because energy flows one-way while nutrients cycle. Statement C is false because nitrogen-fixing bacteria convert N₂ into ammonia/ammonium (NH3/NH4+), not nitrites directly. Statement E describes secondary succession, not primary succession.", "reason_text": null, "grid_key_json": null, "template_type": "five_statement_truth", "assertion_text": null, "correct_option": "B", "cognitive_level": "apply", "question_number": 22, "statements_json": null, "snapshot_created_at": "2026-08-16T19:24:15.014852", "essay_checklist_json": null, "structured_subparts_json": null}	f	\N
2972	210	23	sequential_diagnostic	Identify the correct physiological sequence of events that occurs when blood glucose levels drop significantly below normal in a healthy human.	\N	When blood glucose drops, α cells of the pancreatic islets are stimulated to secrete glucagon. Glucagon acts primarily on the liver to stimulate glycogenolysis (breakdown of glycogen to glucose) and gluconeogenesis, releasing glucose into the bloodstream to restore normal levels.	1	understand	moderate	["A. Hypothalamus detects low glucose \\u2192 Anterior pituitary releases TSH \\u2192 Thyroid secretes thyroxine \\u2192 Glucose oxidation increases", "B. Beta cells of pancreatic islets secrete insulin \\u2192 Glycogenesis is stimulated in skeletal muscles \\u2192 Blood glucose level drops further", "C. Alpha cells of pancreatic islets secrete glucagon \\u2192 Glycogenolysis is stimulated in the liver \\u2192 Glucose is released into the blood", "D. Adrenal cortex secretes aldosterone \\u2192 Distal convoluted tubules reabsorb more sodium \\u2192 Osmotic pressure rises \\u2192 Blood glucose normalizes", "E. Sympathetic nervous system stimulates \\u03b2 cells \\u2192 Glucagon secretion is inhibited \\u2192 Protein synthesis is promoted"]	C	\N	\N	null	{"sequence_steps": ["Low blood glucose detected by \\u03b1 cells", "Secretion of glucagon into the bloodstream", "Targeting of hepatocytes in the liver", "Stimulation of glycogenolysis and gluconeogenesis", "Release of glucose into blood to elevate levels"], "correct_sequence": "1 -> 2 -> 3 -> 4", "colIHeader": "", "colIIHeader": "", "colI": [], "colII": [], "formula": "", "given_values": ""}	null	null	2026-08-16 19:21:24.245834	\N	{"id": 2972, "points": 1.0, "exam_id": 210, "options": ["A. Hypothalamus detects low glucose → Anterior pituitary releases TSH → Thyroid secretes thyroxine → Glucose oxidation increases", "B. Beta cells of pancreatic islets secrete insulin → Glycogenesis is stimulated in skeletal muscles → Blood glucose level drops fu