2964	210	15	combination_grid	Which of the following structural features are adaptations of the mammalian small intestine for efficient nutrient absorption?\nA. Presence of microvilli forming a brush border\nB. Extensive folding of the inner mucosa into circular folds (plicae circulares)\nC. Presence of lacteals within each villus for lipid transport\nD. Dense network of blood capillaries in each villus maintaining a concentration gradient	\N	All listed features (microvilli, circular folds, lacteals, and blood capillaries) maximize surface area and facilitate rapid transport of absorbed water-soluble and lipid-soluble nutrients.	1	apply	moderate	["A. A, B and D only", "B. A, C and D only", "C. B, C and D only", "D. A and C only", "E. A, B, C and D"]	E	\N	\N	[{"code": "A", "text": "Presence of microvilli forming a brush border"}, {"code": "B", "text": "Extensive folding of the inner mucosa into circular folds (plicae circulares)"}, {"code": "C", "text": "Presence of lacteals within each villus for lipid transport"}, {"code": "D", "text": "Dense network of blood capillaries in each villus maintaining a concentration gradient"}]	null	null	null	2026-08-16 19:21:24.245819	\N	{"id": 2964, "points": 1.0, "exam_id": 210, "options": ["A. A, B and D only", "B. A, C and D only", "C. B, C and D only", "D. A and C only", "E. A, B, C and D"], "stem_text": "Which of the following structural features are adaptations of the mammalian small intestine for efficient nutrient absorption?\\nA. Presence of microvilli forming a brush border\\nB. Extensive folding of the inner mucosa into circular folds (plicae circulares)\\nC. Presence of lacteals within each villus for lipid transport\\nD. Dense network of blood capillaries in each villus maintaining a concentration gradient", "difficulty": "moderate", "diagram_url": null, "explanation": "All listed features (microvilli, circular folds, lacteals, and blood capillaries) maximize surface area and facilitate rapid transport of absorbed water-