4327	1025	1	generic_mcq	Which of the following cellular organelles is primarily responsible for the synthesis of lipids and steroid hormones in eukaryotic cells?	\N	The smooth endoplasmic reticulum lacks ribosomes on its outer surface and is the primary site for lipid synthesis, carbohydrate metabolism, and the synthesis of steroid hormones.	1	remember	easy	["A. Rough endoplasmic reticulum", "B. Golgi apparatus", "C. Smooth endoplasmic reticulum", "D. Lysosome", "E. Peroxisome"]	C	\N	\N	null	null	null	null	2026-08-19 20:25:29.694958	\N	{"id": 4327, "points": 1.0, "exam_id": 1025, "options": ["A. Rough endoplasmic reticulum", "B. Golgi apparatus", "C. Smooth endoplasmic reticulum", "D. Lysosome", "E. Peroxisome"], "stem_text": "Which of the following cellular organelles is primarily responsible for the synthesis of lipids and steroid hormones in eukaryotic cells?", "difficulty": "easy", "diagram_url": null, "explanation": "The smooth endoplasmic reticulum lacks ribosomes on its outer surface and is the primary site for lipid synthesis, carbohydrate metabolism, and the synthesis of steroid hormones.", "reason_text": null, "grid_key_json": null, "template_type": "generic_mcq", "assertion_text": null, "correct_option": "C", "cognitive_level": "remember", "question_number": 1, "statements_json": null, "snapshot_created_at": "2026-08-19T20:29:06.389513", "essay_checklist_json": null, "structured_subparts_json": null}	f	\N
4328	1025	2	generic_mcq	Which of the following plant tissues primarily consists of living cells with unevenly thickened primary cell walls that provide mechanical support to growing plant organs?	\N	Collenchyma tissue is composed of living cells with unevenly thickened primary cell walls, providing flexible structural support without restraining growth in young stems and petioles.	1	remember	easy	["A. Collenchyma", "B. Parenchyma", "C. Sclerenchyma", "D. Xylem vessel elements", "E. Tracheids"]	A	\N	\N	null	null	null	null	2026-08-19 20:25:29.694963	\N	{"id": 4328, "points": 1.0, "exam_id": 1025, "options": ["A. Collenchyma", "B. Parenchyma", "C. Sclerenchyma", "D. Xylem vessel elements", "E. Tracheids"], "stem_text": "Which of the following plant tissues primarily consists of living cells with unevenly thickened primary cell walls that provide mechanical support to growing plant organs?", "difficulty": "easy", "diagram_url": null, "explanation": "Collenchyma tissue is composed of living cells with unevenly thickened primary cell walls, providing flexible structural support without restraining growth in young stems and petioles.", "reason_text": null, "grid_key_json": null, "template_type": "generic_mcq", "assertion_text": null, "correct_option": "A", "cognitive_level": "remember", "question_number": 2, "statements_json": null, "snapshot_created_at": "2026-08-19T20:29:06.389561", "essay_checklist_json": null, "structured_subparts_json": null}	f	\N
4329	1025	3	generic_mcq	During the process of oxidative phosphorylation in aerobic respiration, what is the primary role of molecular oxygen ($O_2$)?	\N	Molecular oxygen acts as the final electron acceptor in the electron transport chain, combining with electrons and protons to form water, which allows the continued flow of electrons and maintenance of the proton gradient.	1	understand	easy	["A. Acting as the initial electron donor in the electron transport chain", "B. Serving as the final electron acceptor at the end of the electron transport chain", "C. Directly synthesizing ATP via substrate-level phosphorylation", "D. Donating protons to drive ATP synthase rotation directly", "E. Oxidizing glucose directly in the mitochondrial matrix"]	B	\N	\N	null	null	null	null	2026-08-19 20:25:29.694965	\N	{"id": 4329, "points": 1.0, "exam_id": 1025, "options": ["A. Acting as the initial electron donor in the electron transport chain", "B. Serving as the final electron acceptor at the end of the electron transport chain", "C. Directly synthesizing ATP via substrate-level phosphorylation", "D. Donating protons to drive ATP synthase rotation directly", "E. Oxidizing glucose directly in the mitochondrial matrix"], "stem_text": "During the process of oxidative phosphorylation in aerobic respiration, what is the primary role of molecular oxygen ($O_2$)?", "difficulty": "easy", "diagram_url": null, "explanation": "Molecular oxygen acts as the final electron acceptor in the electron transport chain, combining with electrons and protons to form water, which allows the continued flow of electrons and maintenance of the proton gradient.", "reason_text": null, "grid_key_json": null, "template_type": "generic_mcq", "assertion_text": null, "correct_option": "B", "cognitive_level": "understand", "question_number": 3, "statements_json": null, "snapshot_created_at": "2026-08-19T20:29:06.389579", "essay_checklist_json": null, "structured_subparts_json": null}	f	\N
4330	1025	4	five_statement_truth	Select the correct statement regarding the structural and functional adaptations of the human respiratory system.	\N	Option B is correct because blood arriving at pulmonary capillaries has a higher $P_{CO_2}$ than alveolar air, driving passive diffusion of carbon dioxide out of the blood. Option A is incorrect because external intercostal muscles contract during inspiration. Option C is incorrect because ~98.5% of oxygen binds to hemoglobin. Option D is incorrect because the epiglottis is passive elastic cartilage moved by swallowing mechanics, not active contraction. Option E is incorrect because surfactant decreases surface tension.	1	understand	easy	["A. The contraction of internal intercostal muscles and relaxation of the diaphragm decreases thoracic volume during quiet inspiration.", "B. Most of the oxygen transported in human blood is dissolved directly in the blood plasma.", "C. The partial pressure of carbon dioxide ($P_{CO_2}$) is higher in pulmonary capillaries than in the alveoli, facilitating diffusion of $CO_2$ into the lungs.", "D. The epiglottis is a cartilaginous flap that actively contracts to prevent food entry into the trachea during swallowing.", "E. Surfactant secreted by Type II alveolar cells increases the surface tension of water inside alveoli to prevent collapse."]	C	\N	\N	null	null	null	null	2026-08-19 20:25:29.694967	\N	{"id": 4330, "points": 1.0, "exam_id": 1025, "options": ["A. The contraction of internal intercostal muscles and relaxation of the diaphragm decreases thoracic volume during quiet inspiration.", "B. Most of the oxygen transported in human blood is dissolved directly in the blood plasma.", "C. The partial pressure of carbon dioxide ($P_{CO_2}$) is higher in pulmonary capillaries than in the alveoli, facilitating diffusion of $CO_2$ into the lungs.", "D. The epiglottis is a cartilaginous flap that actively contracts to prevent food entry into the trachea during swallowing.", "E. Surfactant secreted by Type II alveolar cells increases the surface tension of water inside alveoli to prevent collapse."], "stem_text": "Select the correct statement regarding the structural and functional adaptations of the human respiratory system.", "difficulty": "easy", "diagram_url": null, "explanation": "Option B is correct because blood arriving at pulmonary capillaries has a higher $P_{CO_2}$ than alveolar air, driving passive diffusion of carbon dioxide out of the blood. Option A is incorrect because external intercostal muscles contract during inspiration. Option C is incorrect because ~98.5% of oxygen binds to hemoglobin. Option D is incorrect because the epiglottis is passive elastic cartilage moved by swallowing mechanics, not active contraction. Option E is incorrect because surfactant decreases surface tension.", "reason_text": null, "grid_key_json": null, "template_type": "five_statement_truth", "assertion_text": null, "correct_option": "C", "cognitive_level": "understand", "question_number": 4, "statements_json": null, "snapshot_created_at": "2026-08-19T20:29:06.389595", "essay_checklist_json": null, "structured_subparts_json": null}	f	\N
4331	1025	5	matching_column	Match the plant tissue types in Column I with their corresponding primary functions or characteristics in Column II. Select the correct option.	\N	Xylem transports water and minerals (q). Phloem transports organic nutrients (s). Palisade mesophyll performs photosynthesis (p). Epidermis provides protection and gaseous exchange via stomata (r). Thus, a-q, b-s, c-p, d-r.	1	apply	moderate	["A. a-p, b-q, c-r, d-s", "B. a-q, b-p, c-s, d-r", "C. a-r, b-s, c-p, d-q", "D. a-s, b-r, c-q, d-p", "E. a-q, b-s, c-p, d-r"]	E	\N	\N	null	{"colIHeader": "Plant Tissue (Column I)", "colIIHeader": "Function / Characteristic (Column II)", "colI": ["a. Xylem", "b. Phloem", "c. Palisade mesophyll", "d. Epidermis"], "colII": ["p. Primary site of leaf photosynthesis containing abundant chloroplasts", "q. Unidirectional transport of water and dissolved mineral ions", "r. Outer protective cell layer bearing cuticles and stomata", "s. Bidirectional translocation of sugars and organic assimilates"], "formula": "", "given_values": ""}	null	null	2026-08-19 20:25:29.694969	\N	{"id": 4331, "points": 1.0, "exam_id": 1025, "options": ["A. a-p, b-q, c-r, d-s", "B. a-q, b-p, c-s, d-r", "C. a-r, b-s, c-p, d-q", "D. a-s, b-r, c-q, d-p", "E. a-q, b-s, c-p, d-r"], "stem_text": "Match the plant tissue types in Column I with their corresponding primary functions or characteristics in Column II. Select the correct option.", "difficulty": "moderate", "diagram_url": null, "explanation": "Xylem transports water and minerals (q). Phloem transports organic nutrients (s). Palisade mesophyll performs photosynthesis (p). Epidermis provides protection and gaseous exchange via stomata (r). Thus, a-q, b-s, c-p, d-r.", "reason_text": null, "grid_key_json": {"colI": ["a. Xylem", "b. Phloem", "c. Palisade mesophyll", "d. Epidermis"], "colII": ["p. Primary site of leaf photosynthesis containing abundant chloroplasts", "q. Unidirectional transport of water and dissolved mineral ions", "r. Outer pro