4332	1025	6	combination_grid	Consider the following statements regarding ecosystem energy flow and nutrient cycling:\n(A) Energy flows through ecosystems in a one-way path, eventually being dissipated as heat.\n(B) Nutrients are recycled within ecosystems through biogeochemical cycles involving biotic and abiotic components.\n(C) The total gross primary productivity (GPP) of an ecosystem is entirely available for consumption by primary consumers.\n(D) Ecological pyramids of energy are always upright because energy transfer between trophic levels is inefficient.\n\nWhich of the above statements are correct?	\N	Statements A, B, and D are correct. Statement C is incorrect because a significant portion of Gross Primary Productivity (GPP) is used by autotrophs for their own cellular respiration ($R$), leaving Net Primary Productivity (NPP = GPP - R) available for consumers.	1	apply	moderate	["A. (A), (C) and (D) only", "B. (A), (B) and (D) only", "C. (A) and (B) only", "D. (B), (C) and (D) only", "E. All (A), (B), (C) and (D) are correct"]	B	\N	\N	[{"code": "A", "text": "Energy flows through ecosystems in a one-way path, eventually being dissipated as heat."}, {"code": "B", "text": "Nutrients are recycled within ecosystems through biogeochemical cycles involving biotic and abiotic components."}, {"code": "C", "text": "The total gross primary productivity (GPP) of an ecosystem is entirely available for consumption by primary consumers."}, {"code": "D", "text": "Ecological pyramids of energy are always upright because energy transfer between trophic levels is inefficient."}]	null	null	null	2026-08-19 20:25:29.694971	\N	{"id": 4332, "points": 1.0, "exam_id": 1025, "options": ["A. (A), (C) and (D) only", "B. (A), (B) and (D) only", "C. (A) and (B) only", "D. (B), (C) and (D) only", "E. All (A), (B), (C) and (D) are correct"], "stem_text": "Consider the following statements regarding ecosystem energy flow and nutrient cycling:\\n(A) Energy flows through ecosystems in a one-way path, eventually being dissipated as heat.\\n(B) Nutrients are recycled within ecosystems through biogeochemical cycles involving biotic and abiotic components.\\n(C) The total gross primary productivity (GPP) of an ecosystem is entirely available for consumption by primary consumers.\\n(D) Ecological pyramids of energy are always upright because energy transfer between trophic levels is inefficient.\\n\\nWhich of the above statements are correct?", "difficulty": "moderate", "diagram_url": null, "explanation": "Statements A, B, and D are correct. Statement C is incorrect because a significant portion of Gross Primary Productivity (GPP) is used by autotrophs for their own cellular respiration ($R$), leaving Net Primary Productivity (NPP = GPP - R) available for consumers.", "reason_text": null, "grid_key_json": null, "template_type": "combination_grid", "assertion_text": null, "correct_option": "B", "cognitive_level": "apply", "question_number": 6, "statements_json": [{"code": "A", "text": "Energy flows through ecosystems in a one-way path, eventually being dissipated as heat."}, {"code": "B", "text": "Nutrients are recycled within ecosystems through biogeochemical cycles involving biotic and abiotic components."}, {"code": "C", "text": "The total gross primary productivity (GPP) of an ecosystem is entirely available for consumption by primary consumers."}, {"code": "D", "text": "Ecological pyramids of energy are always upright because energy transfer between trophic levels is inefficient."}], "snapshot_created_at": "2026-08-19T20:29:06.389627", "essay_checklist_json": null, "structured_subparts_json": null}	f	\N
4333	1025	7	generic_mcq	If a diploid cell with $2n = 24$ chromosomes undergoes normal meiosis, what will be the number of chromosomes and DNA molecules per cell present at the end of Telophase I?	\N	During anaphase I, homologous chromosomes separate, so each newly formed nucleus at telophase I receives half the total number of chromosomes ($n = 12$). However, because sister chromatids remain joined at the centromere, each chromosome still consists of two sister chromatids, representing 24 DNA molecules in total.	1	apply	moderate	["A. 12 chromosomes and 12 DNA molecules", "B. 24 chromosomes and 24 DNA molecules", "C. 24 chromosomes and 48 DNA molecules", "D. 6 chromosomes and 12 DNA molecules", "E. 12 chromosomes and 24 DNA molecules"]	E	\N	\N	null	null	null	null	2026-08-19 20:25:29.694973	\N	{"id": 4333, "points": 1.0, "exam_id": 1025, "options": ["A. 12 chromosomes and 12 DNA molecules", "B. 24 chromosomes and 24 DNA molecules", "C. 24 chromosomes and 48 DNA molecules", "D. 6 chromosomes and 12 DNA molecules", "E. 12 chromosomes and 24 DNA molecules"], "stem_text": "If a diploid cell with $2n = 24$ chromosomes undergoes normal meiosis, what will be the number of chromosomes and DNA molecules per cell present at the end of Telophase I?", "difficulty": "moderate", "diagram_url": null, "explanation": "During anaphase I, homologous chromosomes separate, so each newly formed nucleus at telophase I receives half the total number of chromosomes ($n = 12$). However, because sister chromatids remain joined at the centromere, each chromosome still consists of two sister chromatids, representing 24 DNA molecules in total.", "reason_text": null, "grid_key_json": null, "template_type": "generic_mcq", "assertion_text": null, "correct_option": "E", "cognitive_level": "apply", "question_number": 7, "statements_json": null, "snapshot_created_at": "2026-08-19T20:29:06.389643", "essay_checklist_json": null, "structured_subparts_json": null}	f	\N
4334	1025	8	five_statement_truth	Which of the following statements regarding the structural features and metabolic processes of plant cells is correct?	\N	Plant cells store carbohydrates mainly as starch, making option D correct. Option A is incorrect because plant cell walls are made of cellulose, not chitin. Option B is incorrect because light-dependent reactions occur in thylakoid membranes, not the stroma. Option C is incorrect because the Calvin cycle occurs in the stroma. Option E is incorrect because cellulose is synthesized at the plasma membrane by cellulose synthase complexes.	1	analyze	moderate	["A. The plant cell wall is composed primarily of chitin to provide mechanical support and resistance to excessive water uptake.", "B. The light-dependent reactions of photosynthesis take place within the stroma of the chloroplast.", "C. The Calvin cycle occurs in the thylakoid membrane where ATP and NADPH are directly consumed.", "D. Plant cells store surplus carbohydrates mainly in the form of starch within specialized plastids.", "E. Cellulose microfibrils in the plant cell wall are synthesized by enzymes located within the vacuolar lumen."]	D	\N	\N	null	null	null	null	2026-08-19 20:25:29.694975	\N	{"id": 4334, "points": 1.0, "exam_id": 1025, "options": ["A. The plant cell wall is composed primarily of chitin to provide mechanical support and resistance to excessive water uptake.", "B. The light-dependent reactions of photosynthesis take place within the stroma of the chloroplast.", "C. The Calvin cycle occurs in the thylakoid membrane where ATP and NADPH are directly consumed.", "D. Plant cells store surplus carbohydrates mainly in the form of starch within specialized plastids.", "E. Cellulose microfibrils in the plant cell wall are synthesized by enzymes located within the vacuolar lumen."], "stem_text": "Which of the following statements regarding the structural features and metabolic processes of plant cells is correct?", "difficulty": "moderate", "diagram_