4335	1025	9	matching_column	Match the major plant groups or evolutionary adaptations in Column I with their corresponding primary defining features or locations in Column II.	\N	Gymnosperms are seed plants with exposed seeds (A-2). Angiosperms are flowering plants with ovules enclosed in an ovary (B-3). The thylakoid membrane hosts the light-dependent reactions (C-4). The stroma is the site of the Calvin cycle (D-1). Thus, the correct matching is A-2, B-3, C-4, D-1.	1	analyze	moderate	["A. A-3, B-2, C-1, D-4", "B. A-2, B-3, C-1, D-4", "C. A-1, B-4, C-2, D-3", "D. A-4, B-1, C-3, D-2", "E. A-2, B-3, C-4, D-1"]	E	\N	\N	null	{"colIHeader": "Plant Group / Adaptation", "colIIHeader": "Defining Feature / Location", "colI": ["A. Gymnosperm", "B. Angiosperm", "C. Thylakoid membrane", "D. Stroma"], "colII": ["1. Site of Calvin cycle in chloroplasts", "2. Seed plant with exposed or 'naked' seeds", "3. Flowering plant whose ovules are enclosed within an ovary", "4. Site of light-dependent reactions of photosynthesis"], "formula": "", "given_values": ""}	null	null	2026-08-19 20:25:29.694976	\N	{"id": 4335, "points": 1.0, "exam_id": 1025, "options": ["A. A-3, B-2, C-1, D-4", "B. A-2, B-3, C-1, D-4", "C. A-1, B-4, C-2, D-3", "D. A-4, B-1, C-3, D-2", "E. A-2, B-3, C-4, D-1"], "stem_text": "Match the major plant groups or evolutionary adaptations in Column I with their corresponding primary defining features or locations in Column II.", "difficulty": "moderate", "diagram_url": null, "explanation": "Gymnosperms are seed plants with exposed seeds (A-2). Angiosperms are flowering plants with ovules enclosed in an ovary (B-3). The thylakoid membrane hosts the light-dependent reactions (C-4). The stroma is the site of the Calvin cycle (D-1). Thus, the correct matching is A-2, B-3, C-4, D-1.", "reason_text": null, "grid_key_json": {"colI": ["A. Gymnosperm", "B. Angiosperm", "C. Thylakoid membrane", "D. Stroma"], "colII": ["1. Site of Calvin cycle in chloroplasts", "2. Seed plant with expo