4336	1025	10	combination_grid	Which of the following statements regarding the general characteristics of Kingdom Plantae is/are correct?\n\nA. Plants are primarily autotrophic organisms that produce organic compounds through photosynthesis.\nB. Most plant cells possess large central vacuoles and cell walls containing cellulose.\nC. Plants exhibit alternation of generations and are capable of active locomotion to capture prey.\nD. Kingdom Plantae includes multicellular eukaryotic organisms that develop from embryos.	\N	Statements A, B, and D are true characteristics of plants. Statement C is false because plants remain attached to their substrate and do not engage in active locomotion to capture prey (a characteristic of animals). Therefore, options A, B, and D only is correct.	1	evaluate	difficult	["A. A, C and D only", "B. A and B only", "C. A, B and D only", "D. C and D only", "E. All A, B, C, D are correct"]	C	\N	\N	[{"code": "A", "text": "Plants are primarily autotrophic organisms that produce organic compounds through photosynthesis.", "is_true": true, "reason": "Plants possess chlorophyll and chloroplasts to capture light energy."}, {"code": "B", "text": "Most plant cells possess large central vacuoles and cell walls containing cellulose.", "is_true": true, "reason": "Cellulose walls and large central vacuoles are characteristic plant cell features."}, {"code": "C", "text": "Plants exhibit alternation of generations and are capable of active locomotion to capture prey.", "is_true": false, "reason": "Plants remain attached to their substrate and are not capable of active locomotion."}, {"code": "D", "text": "Kingdom Plantae includes multicellular eukaryotic organisms that develop from embryos.", "is_true": true, "reason": "Embryonic development is a key characteristic of Kingdom Plantae."}]	null	null	null	2026-08-19 20:25:29.694978	\N	{"id": 4336, "points": 1.0, "exam_id": 1025, "options": ["A. A, C and D only", "B. A and B only", "C. A, B and D only", "D. C an