nation": "Plants are primarily autotrophic, have cellulose-containing cell walls, and remain attached to their substrate, while animals are heterotrophic, lack cell walls, and are capable of locomotion. Thus, option B correctly completes the comparative stem.", "reason_text": null, "grid_key_json": {"colI": [], "colII": [], "formula": "", "colIHeader": "", "colIIHeader": "", "given_values": "", "calculation_steps": ""}, "template_type": "incomplete_stem", "assertion_text": null, "correct_option": "D", "cognitive_level": "evaluate", "question_number": 12, "statements_json": null, "snapshot_created_at": "2026-08-19T20:29:06.389808", "essay_checklist_json": null, "structured_subparts_json": null}	f	\N
4339	1025	13	multi_response_grid	Which of the following statements regarding gene linkage, crossing over, and chromosome mapping in eukaryotic genetics is/are correct?	\N	Statements A, B, and D are correct. Statement C is incorrect because linked genes do not follow independent assortment. Statement E is incorrect because recombination frequency is directly proportional to genetic distance, not inversely proportional.	1	apply	difficult	["Option 1: Statements (A), (B), and (D) only are correct", "Option 2: Statements (A), (C), and (D) only are correct", "Option 3: Statements (A) and (B) only are correct", "Option 4: Statements (C) and (D) only are correct", "Option 5: Any other combination"]	1	\N	\N	[{"code": "A", "text": "Genes located close together on the same chromosome tend to be inherited together and are referred to as linked genes.", "is_true": true, "reason": "Physical proximity on a chromosome restricts independent assortment due to linkage."}, {"code": "B", "text": "In a two-point test cross involving linked genes, the frequency of recombinant offspring is generally lower than that of parental offspring.", "is_true": true, "reason": "Crossing over occurs less frequently than non-crossing over between closely linked loci."}, {"code": "C", "text": "Linked genes always assort independently during meiosis in accordance with Mendel's second law.", "is_true": false, "reason": "Independent assortment only applies to unlinked genes on different chromosomes or far apart on the same chromosome."}, {"code": "D", "text": "Recombination frequency can be used to construct genetic maps representing relative distances between loci on a chromosome.", "is_true": true, "reason": "One map unit (centiMorgan) corresponds to a 1% recombination frequency."}, {"code": "E", "text": "The recombination frequency between two linked genes decreases as the physical distance between them increases.", "is_true": false, "reason": "Recombination frequency increases as the distance between genes increases, up to a maximum of 50%."}]	{"truth": {"A": true, "B": true, "C": false, "D": true, "E": false}, "true_statements": ["A", "B", "D"], "answer_option": "1", "summary": "Statements (A), (B), and (D) only are correct.", "colIHeader": "", "colIIHeader": "", "colI": [], "colII": [], "formula": "", "given_values": ""}	null	null	2026-08-19 20:25:29.694984	\N	{"id": 4339, "points": 1.0, "exam_id": 1025, "options": ["Option 1: Statements (A), (B), and (D) only are correct", "Option 2: Statements (A), (C), and (D) only are correct", "Option 3: Statements (A) and (B) only are correct", "Option 4: Statements (C) and (D) only are correct", "Option 5: Any other combination"], "stem_text": "Which of the following statements regarding gene linkage, crossing over, and chromosome mapping in eukaryotic genetics is/are correct?", "difficulty": "difficult", "diagram_url": null, "explanation": "Statements A, B, and D are correct. Statement C is incorrect because linked genes do not follow independent assortment. Statement E is incorrect because recombination frequency is directly proportional to genetic distance, not inversely proportional.", "reason_text": null, "grid_key_json": {"colI": [], "colII": [], "truth": {"A": true, "B": true, "C": false, "D": true, "E": false}, "formula": "", "summary": "Statements (A), (B), and (D) only are correct.", "colIHeader": "", "colIIHeader": "", "given_values": "", "answer_option": "1", "true_statements": ["A", "B", "D"]}, "template_type": "multi_response_grid", "assertion_text": null, "correct_option": "1", "cognitive_level": "apply", "question_number": 13, "statements_json": [{"code": "A", "text": "Genes located close together on the same chromosome tend to be inherited together and are referred to as linked genes.", "reason": "Physical proximity on a chromosome restricts independent assortment due to linkage.", "is_true": true}, {"code": "B", "text": "In a two-point test cross involving linked genes, the frequency of recombinant offspring is generally lower than that of parental offspring.", "reason": "Crossing over occurs less frequently than non-crossing over between closely linked loci.", "is_true": true}, {"code": "C", "text": "Linked genes always assort independently during meiosis in accordance with Mendel's second law.", "reason": "Independent assortment only applies to unlinked genes on different chromosomes or far apart on the same chromosome.", "is_true": false}, {"code": "D", "text": "Recombination frequency can be used to construct genetic maps representing relative distances between loci on a chromosome.", "reason": "One map unit (centiMorgan) corresponds to a 1% recombination frequency.", "is_true": true}, {"code": "E", "text": "The recombination frequency between two linked genes decreases as the physical distance between them increases.", "reason": "Recombination frequency increases as the distance between genes increases, up to a maximum of 50%.", "is_true": false}], "snapshot_created_at": "2026-08-19T20:29:06.389836", "essay_checklist_json": null, "structured_subparts_json": null}	f	\N
4340	1025	14	multi_response_grid	Which of the following 'hormone - primary target tissue/organ - main physiological effect' combinations in the human endocrine system is/are correct?	\N	Statements A, C, and D correctly match hormones to their target organs and actions. Statement B is incorrect because insulin lowers blood glucose, and Statement E is incorrect because calcitonin lowers blood calcium levels.	1	understand	difficult	["Option 1: Statements (A), (B), and (D) only are correct", "Option 2: Statements (A), (C), and (D) only are correct", "Option 3: Statements (A) and (B) only are correct", "Option 4: Statements (C) and (D) only are correct", "Option 5: Any other combination"]	2	\N	\N	[{"code": "A", "text": "Antidiuretic hormone (ADH) - Kidney distal convoluted tubules and collecting ducts - Increases water reabsorption.", "is_true": true, "reason": "ADH increases the permeability of the distal tubules and collecting ducts to water."}, {"code": "B", "text": "Glucagon - Skeletal muscle and liver - Stimulates the uptake of glucose into cells to reduce blood sugar levels.", "is_true": false, "reason": "Glucagon stimulates glycogenolysis and gluconeogenesis to increase blood glucose, whereas insulin lowers blood sugar."}, {"code": "C", "text": "Thyroxine - Most body cells - Increases basal metabolic rate and oxygen consumption.", "is_true": true, "reason": "Thyroxine regulates overall cellular metabolism across nearly all tissues."}, {"code": "D", "text": "Aldosterone - Kidney distal convoluted tubules - Promotes sodium ion reabsorption and potassium ion excretion.", "is_true": true, "reason": "Aldosterone acts on mineralocorticoid receptors in the distal nephron to retain sodium and water."}, {"code": "E", "text": "Calcitonin - Bones - Stimulates osteoclast activity to release calcium ions into the blood.", "is_true": false, "reason": "Calcitonin inhibits osteoclasts and promotes calcium deposition in bones, lowering blood calcium levels."}]	{"truth": {"A": true, "B": false, "C": true, "D": true, "E": false}, "true_statements": ["A", "C", "D"], "answer_option": "2", "summary": "Statements (A), (C), and (D) only are correct.", "colIHeader": "", "colIIHeader": "", "colI": [], "colII": [], "formula": "", "given_values": ""}	null	null	2026-08-19 20:25:29.694985	\N	{"id": 4340, "points": 1.0, "exam_id": 1025, "options": ["Option 1: Statements (A), (B), and (D) only are correct", "Option 2: Statements (A), (C), and (D) only are correct", "Option 3: Statements (A) and (B) only are correct", "Option 4: Statements (C) and (D) only are correct", "Option 5: Any other combination"], "stem_text": "Which of the following 'hormone - primary target tissue/organ - main physiological effect' combinations in the human endocrine system is/are correct?", "difficulty": "difficult", "diagram_url": null, "explanation": "Statements A, C, and D correctly match hormones to their target organs and actions. Statement B is incorrect because insulin lowers blood glucose, and Statement E is incorrect because calcitonin lowers blood calcium levels.", "reason_text": null, "grid_key_json": {"colI": [], "colII": [], "truth": {"A": true, "B": false, "C": true, "D": true, "E": false}, "formula": "", "summary": "Statements (A), (C), and (D) only are correct.", "colIHeader": "", "colIIHeader": "", "given_values": "", "answer_option": "2", "true_statements": ["A", "C", "D"]}, "template_type": "multi_response_grid", "assertion_text": null, "correct_option": "2", "cognitive_level": "understand", "question_number": 14, "statements_json": [{"code": "A", "text": "Antidiuretic hormone (ADH) - Kidney distal convoluted tubules and collecting ducts - Increases water reabsorption.", "reason": "ADH increases the permeability of the distal tubules and collecting ducts to water.", "is_true": true}, {"code": "B", "text": "Glucagon - Skeletal muscle and liver - Stimulates the uptake of glucose into cells to reduce blood sugar levels.", "reason": "Glucagon stimulates glycogenolysis and gluconeogenesis to increase blood glucose, whereas insulin lowers blood sugar.", "is_true": false}, {"code": "C", "text": "Thyroxine - Most body cells - Increases basal metabolic rate and oxygen consumption.", "reason": "Thyroxine regulates overall cellular metabolism across nearly all tissues.", "is_true": true}, {"code": "D", "text": "Aldosterone - Kidney distal convoluted tubules - Promotes sodium ion reabsorption and potassium ion excretion.", "reason": "Aldosterone acts on mineralocorticoid receptors in the distal nephron to retain sodium and water.", "is_true": true}, {"code": "E", "text": "Calcitonin - Bones - Stimulates osteoclast activity to release calcium ions into the blood.", "reason": "Calcitonin inhibits osteoclasts and promotes calcium deposition in bones, lowering blood calcium levels.", "is_true": false}], "snapshot_created_at": "2026-08-19T20:29:06.389854", "essay_checklist_json": null, "structured_subparts_json": null}	f	\N
4341	1025	15	multi_response_grid	Which of the following statements regarding the structural features and chemical properties of nucleic acids is/are correct?	\N	Statements A, B, and D are correct regarding nucleic acid structure and base pairing rules. Statement C is incorrect because RNA contains uracil instead of thymine, and Statement E is incorrect because DNA strands are antiparallel, not parallel.	1	understand	difficult	["Option 1: Statements (A), (B), and (D) only are correct", "Option 2: Statements (A), (C), and (D) only are correct", "Option 3: Statements (A) and (B) only are correct", "Option 4: Statements (C) and (D) only are correct", "Option 5: Any other combination"]	1	\N	\N	[{"code": "A", "text": "DNA molecules consist of two polynucleotide chains wound around a central axis in a double helix.", "is_true": true, "reason": "Standard Watson-Crick structure of double-stranded DNA."}, {"code": "B", "text": "Adenine pairs with thymine via two hydrogen bonds in DNA molecules.", "is_true": true, "reason": "Purine-pyrimidine complementary base pairing establishes two hydrogen bonds between A and T."}, {"code": "C", "text": "RNA molecules contain thymine as one of their four nitrogenous bases.", "is_true": false, "reason": "RNA contains uracil (U) instead of thymine (T)."}, {"code": "D", "text": "The backbone of a nucleic acid strand is composed of alternating pentose sugar and phosphate groups.", "is_true": true, "reason": "Phosphodiester bonds link the 3' carbon of one sugar to the 5' carbon of the next, forming the sugar-phosphate backbone."}, {"code": "E", "text": "The two strands of a DNA double helix run in the same parallel 5' to 3' direction.", "is_true": false, "reason": "DNA strands are antiparallel; one runs 5' to 3' and the complementary strand runs 3' to 5'."}]	{"truth": {"A": true, "B": true, "C": false, "D": true, "E": false}, "true_statements": ["A", "B", "D"], "answer_option": "1", "summary": "Statements (A), (B), and (D) only are correct.", "