e": "D", "text": "The backbone of a nucleic acid strand is composed of alternating pentose sugar and phosphate groups.", "reason": "Phosphodiester bonds link the 3' carbon of one sugar to the 5' carbon of the next, forming the sugar-phosphate backbone.", "is_true": true}, {"code": "E", "text": "The two strands of a DNA double helix run in the same parallel 5' to 3' direction.", "reason": "DNA strands are antiparallel; one runs 5' to 3' and the complementary strand runs 3' to 5'.", "is_true": false}], "snapshot_created_at": "2026-08-19T20:29:06.389871", "essay_checklist_json": null, "structured_subparts_json": null}	f	\N
4342	1025	16	structured_subparts	The living world exhibits a remarkable degree of organization spanning from molecular components to the biosphere. Understanding the nature, scope, and structural hierarchies of life forms—ranging from unicellular organisms to complex multicellular systems—is fundamental to biological science.	\N	\N	40	recommended	balanced	null	A	\N	\N	null	null	[{"id": "node_1787171248947_1pi40j", "label": "", "format_type": "structured_direct_recall", "points": 10, "children": [{"id": "node_1787171248947_skyiq4", "label": "", "format_type": "structured_direct_recall", "points": 2, "prompt": "State the two Greek roots from which the word 'biology' is derived and give their literal meanings.", "model_answer": "The word biology is derived from 'Bios' meaning life, and 'Logos' meaning study or knowledge.", "marking_points": [{"criterion": "Identified 'Bios' meaning life", "points": 1}, {"criterion": "Identified 'Logos' meaning study or knowledge", "points": 1}], "diagram_info": {"requires_image": false}, "children": []}, {"id": "node_1787171248947_pkcwyn", "label": "", "format_type": "structured_direct_recall", "points": 2, "prompt": "Name two acellular biological entities that are investigated in biology despite not being independently regarded as living organisms.", "model_answer": "Viruses and prions (or viroids).", "marking_points": [{"criterion": "Named viruses correctly", "points": 1}, {"criterion": "Named prions or viroids correctly", "points": 1}], "diagram_info": {"requires_image": false}, "children": []}, {"id": "node_1787171248947_banf1q", "label": "", "format_type": "structured_conceptual", "points": 6, "prompt": "Explain why biology is classified as an empirical science and state two key characteristics of its scientific nature.", "model_answer": "Biology is an empirical science because biological knowledge is developed and evaluated using observations, measurements, experiments, and concrete evidence. Two key characteristics are that biology is evidence-based and that it is constantly developing as new evidence emerges.", "marking_points": [{"criterion": "Explained empirical science based on observation, measurement, and experimentation", "points": 3}, {"criterion": "Stated two key characteristics (evidence-based and constantly developing)", "points": 3}], "diagram_info": {"requires_image": false}, "children": []}], "prompt": "", "marking_points": [], "diagram_info": {"requires_image": false}}, {"id": "node_1787171248947_v36dfe", "label": "", "format_type": "structured_comparison", "points": 14, "children": [{"id": "node_1787171248947_de5k2a", "label": "", "format_type": "structured_comparison", "points": 6, "prompt": "Compare and contrast prokaryotic cells and eukaryotic cells based on nuclear organization and membrane-bound organelles.", "model_answer": "Prokaryotic cells generally lack a true membrane-bound nucleus and membrane-bound organelles. Eukaryotic cells possess a distinct membrane-bound nucleus containing genetic material and various membrane-bound organelles such as mitochondria and the endoplasmic reticulum.", "marking_points": [{"criterion": "Correctly described nuclear differences between prokaryotic and eukaryotic cells", "points": 3}, {"criterion": "Correctly described the presence versus absence of membrane-bound organelles", "points": 3}], "comparison_header_1": "Prokaryotic Cells", "comparison_header_2": "Eukaryotic Cells", "comparison_pairs": [{"criterion": "Nuclear structure", "value_1": "Lacks a membrane-bound nucleus (nucleoid region present)", "value_2": "Contains a distinct membrane-bound nucleus"}, {"criterion": "Membrane-bound organelles", "value_1": "Absent", "value_2": "Present (e.g., mitochondria, Golgi apparatus)"}], "diagram_info": {"requires_image": false}, "children": []}, {"id": "node_1787171248947_zeaw5b", "label": "", "format_type": "structured_conceptual", "points": 4, "prompt": "Explain how cell specialization enhances the efficiency of complex functions in multicellular organisms compared to unicellular organisms.", "model_answer": "In multicellular organisms, different cells differentiate and specialize to perform specific tasks (such as red blood cells for oxygen transport or neurons for impulse transmission). This division of labor allows the organism to perform complex physiological functions with high efficiency, whereas a single cell in a unicellular organism must perform all essential life functions independently.", "marking_points": [{"criterion": "Described division of labor through cell specialization in multicellular organisms", "points": 2}, {"criterion": "Contrasted with unicellular organisms where one cell performs all life functions", "points": 2}], "diagram_info": {"requires_image": false}, "children": []}, {"id": "node_1787171248947_6p1jon", "label": "", "format_type": "structured_sequential", "points": 4, "prompt": "Outline the biological hierarchy of structural organization from the organelle level up to the organism level in multicellular eukaryotes.", "model_answer": "Organelles coordinate within a cell, cells group to form tissues, tissues combine to form organs, organs operate within organ systems, and organ systems constitute the complete multicellular organism.", "marking_points": [{"criterion": "Accurately ordered the levels from organelle to organ system", "points": 2}, {"criterion": "Completed the sequence up to the multicellular organism level", "points": 2}], "sequence_items": ["Organelle level", "Cellular level", "Tissue level", "Organ and Organ System level"], "diagram_info": {"requires_image": false}, "children": []}], "prompt": "", "marking_points": [], "diagram_info": {"requires_image": false}}, {"id": "node_1787171248947_ih1v5a", "label": "", "format_type": "structured_conceptual", "points": 16, "children": [{"id": "node_1787171248947_l0jfuw", "label": "", "format_type": "structured_matrix", "points": 8, "prompt": "Complete the following table identifying specific eukaryotic organelles and their primary cellular functions.", "model_answer": "Mitochondria function in aerobic respiration and ATP production. The nucleus contains the majority of the genetic material. Chloroplasts are responsible for photosynthesis in plants. Lysosomes contain digestive enzymes for intracellular breakdown.", "marking_points": [{"criterion": "Correctly matched functions for Mitochondria and Nucleus", "points": 4}, {"criterion": "Correctly matched functions for Chloroplasts and Lysosomes", "points": 4}], "matrix_data": {"col_headers": ["Organelle / Structure", "Primary Cellular Function"], "rows": [{"item": "Mitochondria", "expected": "Site of aerobic respiration and ATP production"}, {"item": "Nucleus", "expected": "Houses the genetic material and controls cellular activities"}, {"item": "Chloroplast", "expected": "Site of photosynthesis in photosynthetic eukaryotic cells"}, {"item": "Lysosome", "expected": "Intracellular digestion and breakdown of waste materials"}]}, "diagram_info": {"requires_image": false}, "children": []}, {"id": "node_1787171248947_220h2o", "label": "", "format_type": "structured_conceptual", "points": 8, "prompt": "Discuss why biological knowledge is considered dynamic and not permanently unchangeable, citing the role of technological advancements in microscopy and molecular biology.", "model_answer": "Scientific knowledge evolves as new evidence is gathered. Advances in technology, such as improvements in high-resolution light and electron microscopy and DNA sequencing techniques, allow scientists to visualize cellular ultrastructures and analyze genetic relationships with unprecedented precision. This new empirical evidence frequently leads to the modification, refinement, or replacement of pre-existing biological classifications and theories.", "marking_points": [{"criterion": "Explained that scientific knowledge is open to modification based on new evidence", "points": 4}, {"criterion": "Highlighted the specific contributions of microscopy, genetics, and DNA sequencing", "points": 4}], "diagram_info": {"requires_image": false}, "children": []}], "prompt": "", "marking_points": [], "diagram_info": {"requires_image": false}}]	null	2026-08-19 20:28:02.570492	\N	{"id": 4342, "points": 40.0, "exam_id": 1025, "options": null, "stem_text": "The living world exhibits a remarkable degree of organization spanning from molecular components to the biosphere. Understanding the nature, scope, and structural hierarchies of life forms—ranging from unicellular organisms to complex multicellular systems—is fundamental to biological science.", "difficulty": "balanced", "diagram_url": null, "explanation": null, "reason_text": null, "grid_key_json": null, "template_type": "structured_subparts", "assertion_text": null, "correct_option": "A", "cognitive_level": "recommended", "question_number": 16, "statements_json": null, "snapshot_created_at": "2026-08-19T20:29:06.389889", "essay_checklist_json": null, "structured_subparts_json": [{"id": "node_1787171248947_1pi40j", "label": "", "points": 10, "prompt": "", "children": [{"id": "node_1787171248947_skyiq4", "label": "", "points": 2, "prompt": "State the two Greek roots from which the word 'biology' is derived and give their literal meanings.", "children": [], "format_type": "structured_direct_recall", "diagram_info": {"requires_image": false}, "model_answer": "The word biology is derived from 'Bios' meaning life, and 'Logos' meaning study or knowledge.", "marking_points": [{"points": 1, "criterion": "Identified 'Bios' meaning life"}, {"points": 1, "criterion": "Identified 'Logos' meaning study or knowledge"}]}, {"id": "node_1787171248947_pkcwyn", "label": "", "points": 2, "prompt": "Name two acellular biological entities that are investigated in biology despite not being independently regarded as living organisms.", "children": [], "format_type": "structured_direct_recall", "diagram_info": {"requires_image": false}, "model_answer": "Viruses and prions (or viroids).", "marking_points": [{"points": 1, "criterion": "Named viruses correctly"}, {"points": 1, "criterion": "Named prions or viroids correctly"}]}, {"id": "node_1787171248947_banf1q", "label": "", "points": 6, "prompt": "Explain why biology is classified as an empirical science and state two key characteristics of its scientific nature.", "children": [], "format_type": "structured_conceptual", "diagram_info": {"requires_image": false}, "model_answer": "Biology is an empirical science because biological knowledge is developed and evaluated using observations, measurements, experiments, and concrete evidence. Two key characteristics are that biology is evidence-based and that it is constantly developing as new evidence emerges.", "marking_points": [{"points": 3, "criterion": "Explained empirical science based on observation, measurement, and experimentation"}, {"points": 3, "criterion": "Stated two key characteristics (evidence-based and constantly developing)"}]}], "format_type": "structured_direct_recall", "diagram_info": {"requires_image": false}, "marking_points": []}, {"id": "node_1787171248947_v36dfe", "label": "", "points": 14, "prompt": "", "children": [{"id": "node_1787171248947_de5k2a", "label": "", "points": 6, "prompt": "Compare and contrast prokaryotic cells and eukaryotic cells based on nuclear organization and membrane-bound organelles.", "children": [], "format_type": "structured_comparison", "diagram_info": {"requires_image": false}, "model_answer": "Prokaryotic cells generally lack a true membrane-bound nucleus and membrane-bound organelles. Eukaryotic cells possess a distinct membrane-bound nucleus containing genetic material and various membrane-bound organelles such as mitochondria and the endoplasmic reticulum.", "marking_points": [{"points": 3, "criterion": "Correctly described nuclear differences between prokaryotic and eukaryotic cells"}, {"points": 3, "criterion": "Correctly described the presence versus absence of membrane-bound organelles"}], "compariso