4468	1025	19	five_statement_truth	Which of the following statements regarding human endocrine system is correct?	\N	Aldosterone acts on the distal tubules and collecting ducts to increase sodium and water reabsorption. Calcitonin is secreted by thyroid C cells (not parathyroid). Posterior pituitary stores/releases ADH and oxytocin but does not synthesize them. Insulin is produced by β cells. Thyroxine increases basal metabolic rate.	1	apply	moderate	["A. Calcitonin secreted by the parathyroid glands decreases blood calcium levels.", "B. Aldosterone promotes the reabsorption of sodium ions and water in the distal convoluted tubules and collecting ducts of nephrons.", "C. The posterior pituitary gland synthesizes oxytocin and antidiuretic hormone (ADH).", "D. Insulin is produced by \\u03b1 cells of the Islets of Langerhans in the pancreas.", "E. Thyroxine decreases basal metabolic rate in target tissues."]	B	\N	\N	null	null	null	null	2026-08-23 14:54:15.927708	\N	\N	f	\N
4469	1025	20	combination_grid	Consider the following statements regarding cellular respiration:\nA. Glycolysis occurs in the cytoplasm and requires oxygen to proceed.\nB. The Krebs cycle takes place in the mitochondrial matrix and produces NADH and FADH₂.\nC. Oxidative phosphorylation involves the electron transport chain and chemiosmosis.\nD. Fermentation yields a net gain of 36 ATP molecules per glucose molecule.	\N	Statement A is incorrect because glycolysis is anaerobic and does not require oxygen. Statement B is correct; the Krebs cycle occurs in the mitochondrial matrix producing electron carriers. Statement C is correct; oxidative phosphorylation uses the ETC and chemiosmosis. Statement D is incorrect because fermentation yields only 2 ATP molecules per glucose.	1	evaluate	difficult	["A. A and B only", "B. B and C only", "C. A, C and D only", "D. B, C and D only", "E. A, B and C only"]	B	\N	\N	[{"code": "A", "text": "Glycolysis occurs in the cytoplasm and requires oxygen to proceed.", "is_true": false}, {"code": "B", "text": "The Krebs cycle takes place in the mitochondrial matrix and produces NADH and FADH\\u2082.", "is_true": true}, {"code": "C", "text": "Oxidative phosphorylation involves the electron transport chain and chemiosmosis.", "is_true": true}, {"code": "D", "text": "Fermentation yields a net gain of 36 ATP molecules per glucose molecule.", "is_true": false}]	null	null	null	2026-08-23 14:54:15.927713	\N	\N	f	\N
