bsorption of all glucose, amino acids, and most water/salts' and 'Distal Convoluted Tubule: Selective water and ion reabsorption.'", "feedback": "Correctly matched and described both segments according to the requirements."}, {"criterion_id": "node_1786909059509_tqoddl", "description": "Discuss how the kidneys compensate for prolonged metabolic acidosis in the human body.", "awarded": 2.0, "maximum": 8.0, "evidence": "Student mentioned CKDu and clearance formula, but did not discuss metabolic acidosis compensation mechanisms (H+ secretion, bicarbonate generation/reabsorption).", "feedback": "Acidosis compensation was not discussed; unrelated information regarding CKDu was provided."}], "feedback": "The student demonstrated good knowledge of the loop of Henle, collecting duct function under dehydration, and the basic functions of the proximal and distal convoluted tubules. However, several sections (such as podocytes, renin, structural adaptations of the PCT, vasa recta, and metabolic acidosis) were either omitted or incorrectly addressed.", "is_fallback": false}	{"subpart_marks": 35.0}	35	Q1 Nephron: Awarded 35.0/40 based on subpart correctness.	0	3	35	35
