587	586	During which phase of the cell cycle does the replication of nuclear DNA take place?	MCQ	["A. G\\u2081 phase", "B. G\\u2082 phase", "C. S phase", "D. M phase", "E. G\\u2080 phase"]	C	DNA replication and chromosome duplication occur exclusively during the Synthesis (S) phase of interphase in the cell cycle.	1	EASY	REMEMBER	\N	APPROVED	al_exam	210	G.C.E. A/L Biology Paper I (First)	2026-08-18 06:09:31.506873	["G.C.E. A/L Biology Paper I (First)", "generic_mcq"]	\N	60	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	f	\N	\N	\N	\N
588	587	How does an uncompetitive enzyme inhibitor typically affect the maximum reaction velocity (Vmax) and the Michaelis constant (Km) of an enzyme-catalyzed reaction?	MCQ	["A. Increases Vmax and increases Km", "B. Does not affect Vmax but increases Km", "C. Decreases Vmax and increases Km", "D. Decreases Vmax and decreases Km", "E. Increases Vmax and decreases Km"]	D	Uncompetitive inhibitors bind only to the enzyme-substrate complex, lowering both Vmax (because product formation is hindered) and apparent Km (increasing apparent substrate affinity due to trapping the ES complex).	1	EASY	UNDERSTAND	\N	APPROVED	al_exam	210	G.C.E. A/L Biology Paper I (First)	2026-08-18 06:09:31.513814	["G.C.E. A/L Biology Paper I (First)", "generic_mcq"]	\N	60	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	f	\N	\N	\N	\N
589	588	Which of the following metabolic pathways occurs in the cytoplasm of eukaryotic cells under both aerobic and anaerobic conditions?	MCQ	["A. Krebs cycle", "B. Oxidative phosphorylation", "C. Beta-oxidation", "D. Alcoholic fermentation", "E. Glycolysis"]	E	Glycolysis takes place in the cytosol of cells and does not require oxygen, functioning as the initial stage for both aerobic respiration and fermentation pathways.	1	EASY	UNDERSTAND	\N	APPROVED	al_exam	210	G.C.E. A/L Biology Paper I (First)	2026-08-18 06:09:31.518404	["G.C.E. A/L Biology Paper I (First)", "generic_mcq"]	\N	60	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	f	\N	\N	\N	\N
