602	601	Which of the following statements regarding the human nervous system and nerve impulse transmission are correct?\n\nA. The resting membrane potential of a neuron is maintained primarily by the sodium-potassium pump actively transporting 3 Na⁺ out and 2 K⁺ in.\nB. During depolarization of an axon membrane, voltage-gated potassium channels open rapidly while sodium channels remain closed.\nC. Saltatory conduction occurs in myelinated nerve fibers where action potentials jump from one Node of Ranvier to the next.\nD. Neurotransmitters are released from the presynaptic knob into the synaptic cleft via exocytosis upon the influx of calcium ions.	MCQ	["A. A, B and C only", "B. B, C and D only", "C. A, B and D only", "D. A, C and D only", "E. All A, B, C and D are correct"]	D	Statement A is correct (sodium-potassium pump mechanism). Statement B is incorrect because during depolarization, voltage-gated sodium channels open rapidly, not potassium channels (potassium channels open during repolarization). Statement C is correct (saltatory conduction in myelinated fibers). Statement D is correct (calcium-mediated exocytosis of neurotransmitters). Therefore, A, C, and D are correct.	1	MEDIUM	APPLY	\N	APPROVED	al_exam	210	G.C.E. A/L Biology Paper I (First)	2026-08-18 06:09:31.583214	["G.C.E. A/L Biology Paper I (First)", "combination_grid"]	\N	60	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	f	\N	\N	\N	\N
603	602	In a patient suffering from a specific endocrine disorder, laboratory tests reveal abnormally high levels of adrenocorticotropic hormone (ACTH) in the blood, coupled with low levels of cortisol. Which of the following conditions best describes this physiological state?	MCQ	["A. Primary hypercortisolism (Cushing's disease due to adrenal adenoma)", "B. Secondary hypercortisolism due to anterior pituitary tumor", "C. Diabetes insipidus resulting from posterior pituitary dysfunction", "D. Hyperthyroidism caused by Graves' disease", "E. Primary hypocortisolism (Addison's disease) causing a loss of negative feedback on the anterior pituitary"]	E	In primary hypocortisolism (Addison's disease), the adrenal cortex fails to secrete cortisol. The resulting low blood cortisol levels remove the normal negative feedback inhibition on the hypothalamus and anterior pituitary, leading to elevated secretion of ACTH.	1	MEDIUM	APPLY	\N	APPROVED	al_exam	210	G.C.E. A/L Biology Paper I (First)	2026-08-18 06:09:31.587258	["G.C.E. A/L Biology Paper I (First)", "generic_mcq"]	\N	60	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	f	\N	\N	\N	\N
604	603	Match the animal hormones in Column I with their respective primary target organs or mechanism of action in Column II, as described in the G.C.E. A/L Biology curriculum.	MCQ	["A. P-(iii), Q-(iv), R-(i), S-(ii)", "B. P-(iv), Q-(i), R-(ii), S-(iii)", "C. P-(ii), Q-(iii), R-(i), S-(iv)", "D. P-(i), Q-(ii), R-(iv), S-(iii)", "E. P-(iv), Q-(iii), R-(ii), S-(i)"]	A	P. Calcitonin targets bones to inhibit osteoclast activity (iii). Q. Antidiuretic hormone (ADH) targets the collecting ducts of the kidney (iv). R. Thyroxine targets general body tissues to stimulate basal metabolic rate (i). S. Progesterone targets the endometrium of the uterus to maintain the uterine lining (ii).	1	MEDIUM	UNDERSTAND	\N	APPROVED	al_exam	210	G.C.E. A/L Biology Paper I (First)	2026-08-18 06:09:31.591697	["G.C.E. A/L Biology Paper I (First)", "matching_column"]	\N	60	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	f	\N	\N	\N	\N
605	604	Which of the following statements regarding environmental biology, ecological pyramids, and biogeochemical cycles in Sri Lankan ecosystems is correct?	MCQ	["A. In all aquatic ecosystems, the ecological pyramid of biomass is invariably upright because producers have a shorter life span and higher turnover rate than consumers.", "B. Biological magnification (biomagnification) results in higher concentrations of persistent lipophilic toxins in organisms at higher trophic levels.", "C. The flow of energy through an ecosystem is cyclical, whereas nutrients follow a one-way unidirectional flow.", "D. Nitrogen fixation converts atmospheric nitrogen gas directly into nitrites (NO2-) which are then absorbed by plant roots.", "E. Primary succession always begins on a pre-existing soil substrate after a forest fire or agricultural clearing."]	B	Statement D is correct: non-biodegradable, lipid-soluble toxins (such as heavy metals or persistent pesticides) undergo biomagnification, increasing in concentration at higher trophic levels. Statement A is false because aquatic biomass pyramids can be inverted (phytoplankton biomass < zooplankton biomass). Statement B is false because energy flows one-way while nutrients cycle. Statement C is false because nitrogen-fixing bacteria convert N₂ into ammonia/ammonium (NH3/NH4+), not nitrites directly. Statement E describes secondary succession, not primary succession.	1	MEDIUM	APPLY	\N	APPROVED	al_exam	210	G.C.E. A/L Biology Paper I (First)	2026-08-18 06:09:31.598172	["G.C.E. A/L Biology Paper I (First)", "five_statement_truth"]	\N	60	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	f	\N	\N	\N	\N
606	605	Identify the correct physiological sequence of events that occurs when blood glucose levels drop significantly below normal in a healthy human.	MCQ	["A. Hypothalamus detects low glucose \\u2192 Anterior pituitary releases TSH \\u2192 Thyroid secretes thyroxine \\u2192 Glucose oxidation increases", "B. Beta cells of pancreatic islets secrete insulin \\u2192 Glycogenesis is stimulated in skeletal muscles \\u2192 Blood glucose level drops further", "C. Alpha cells of pancreatic islets secrete glucagon \\u2192 Glycogenolysis is stimulated in the liver \\u2192 Glucose is released into the blood", "D. Adrenal cortex secretes aldosterone \\u2192 Distal convoluted tubules reabsorb more sodium \\u2192 Osmotic pressure rises \\u2192 Blood glucose normalizes", "E. Sympathetic nervous system stimulates \\u03b2 cells \\u2192 Glucagon secretion is inhibited \\u2192 Protein synthesis is promoted"]	C	When blood glucose drops, α cells of the pancreatic islets are stimulated to secrete glucagon. Glucagon acts primarily on the liver to stimulate glycogenolysis (breakdown of glycogen to glucose) and gluconeogenesis, releasing glucose into the bloodstream to restore normal levels.	1	MEDIUM	UNDERSTAND	\N	APPROVED	al_exam	210	G.C.E. A/L Biology Paper I (First)	2026-08-18 06:09:31.602355	["G.C.E. A/L Biology Paper I (First)", "sequential_diagnostic"]	\N	60	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	f	\N	\N	\N	\N
